Z||000000||mrgone||07-12-2001||01:31 PM||||my car has the yucky warped center console.<P>should i take off the vent there and use epoxy and c-clamp it?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroint_1.JPG"> <p>[This message has been edited by mrgone (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||286SE'S||07-12-2001||02:31 PM||||Yes that is the usual way. It is much easier if you pull that whole part off the car and do it on a table. <BR>Remove the ashtrays and take out the 4 -7mm<BR>bolts that hold the shift plate down. unscrew the shift knob and pull the plate off. There are three 7mm screws holding down the bottom of the radio/heater vinyl. After you remove the face plate (4 15torx) there are two more 7mm screws to remove. The whole vinyl casing will now pull out for regluing. <BR>Be sure to clean both surfaces very well. There will be lots of yellow dried foam crap that will get in your new glue if you don't remove it. I actually dug out some of it so that the vinyl would have less reason to pull up again. Getting the reglue flat and even is important as you will always be looking at this spot. I used a flat 1"x2" board along the top and a clamp at each end. Spring loaded clothspins to hold the fresh glue area down.<BR>While that shift plate is off; give it some attention too. It looks a little warped in the picture.<BR>You may also want to search the archives on this subject. It is a repair that all Fiero owners have to do. My first car, the dealer had used rivits to 'repair' it. looked like crap. My brother used duct tape on his, even worse.<p>[This message has been edited by 286SE'S (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||07-12-2001||04:09 PM||||I bought this $20/oz super glue in a car related expo one year ago which proved to be great to fix that. Took my new Formula center console that was literally in pieces and all warped up and was able to put it like new in just 30 minutes. Also fixed a warp like that but in the right side instead of top. If interested I can get the name of the glue but not sure where they sell it.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||07-12-2001||04:17 PM||||what i did for all my; trim was by using super glue.  i went to a hobby shop and got some accelerator(just go in and ask for super glue accelerator)  and some glue.  take a razor and carefully cut out the foam on the edges and apply the super glue,  then spray it with the accelerator.  the key is to use a flat edge(i used an old cd case) to hold the edges down to they dont look wavy.  i did mine a while ago and they look great.  doesnt take too long either.  only problem was gettin the glue off my fingertips.  but a little acetone works for that.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
